    "intro_narrative": "The rain lashes against the reinforced glass of Precinct 42. You are Lead Detective Vance, and you've just walked into the evidence room after a grueling 48-hour shift. The infamous 'Cipher Killer' has left behind a trail of highly encrypted digital footprints and locked physical evidence. The precinct's systems have been scrambled, and standard protocols are useless. Your objective is clear: navigate the web of corrupted data, crack the intricate mathematical cyphers, and access the final piece of evidence that will blow this case wide open. Time is running out before the killer's automated scripts wipe the precinct's servers clean. You must rely on your wits, the precinct's specialized forensic tools, and the scattered clues left behind to unmask the culprit. Examine everything carefully; in this line of work, every hash, code, and locked container tells a story.",
    "narrative_style": "detective"
  },
